    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Gunnar Henderson** anchoring the lineup as the clear top play, boasting an elite score of 81.88. **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from a prime matchup against Warren in a favorable park environment, with his dynamic platoon advantage and high-leverage spot in the #3 hole providing a massive ceiling. He is joined at the top of the efficiency charts by **Jackson Merrill** (75.27) and **Kyle Tucker** (74.09). **Jackson Merrill** receives a notable boost from wind patterns and a favorable SP xERA of 4.94, while **Kyle Tucker** remains a high-floor start despite a slight downgrade from his #7 position. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** also projects strongly (73.66) due to the soft matchup against Bassitt, where favorable park factors and SP vulnerability align to elevate his expected output significantly above his baseline projection.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Wade Meckler**, who fell just short of the lineup with a score of 46.94. While **Wade Meckler** provides the benefit of a #1 batting order slot\u2014which typically boosts on-base opportunities\u2014his lower raw efficiency in this specific matchup against Pecko meant he was edged out by high-scoring utility options like **Sam Antonacci**, whose platoon advantage and park factors nudged him ahead. We are currently navigating the absences of **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, **Luis Robert Jr.**, and **Jordan Westburg**, whose placement on the IL continues to constrain our depth, particularly in the outfield and corner infield.\n\nRisk management remains a priority today, specifically regarding **Miguel Vargas** and **Heliot Ramos**. Both players face starters who demonstrate high success in controlling the running game (53% and 63% hold rates, respectively); given our organizational emphasis on Stolen Bases, this suppresses their overall utility score despite otherwise solid matchups. Furthermore, while **Drake Baldwin** (57.94) and **Liam Hicks** (54.32) provide serviceable production behind the dish, they operate in the marginal range. We will continue to monitor lineups for **Jacob Wilson**, **Josh Jung**, **Curtis Mead**, and **Luis Lara** as we look to preserve our remaining game caps for higher-leverage opportunities later in the week.",
